---
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base title="About | Jeremy Hoover" description="Jeremy Hoover builds product systems, design workflows, and AI-powered tools. He is a senior content designer at Microsoft and an instructor at the UX Content Collective.">

  <section class="section about-page">
    <header class="about-hero">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <a href={`${base}/`} class="hero-back"><span class="back-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Back to homepage</span></a>
        <div class="about-id">
          <img src={`${base}/images/jeremy-hoover.jpg`} alt="" width="88" height="88" />
          <div>
            <h1>Jeremy Hoover</h1>
            <p class="subtitle">Senior Content Designer at Microsoft and UXCC instructor</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="about-content">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <div class="about-body">
        <p>
          I design customer-facing developer tools, content experiences, and product workflows, as
          well as internal systems that teams depend on. At Microsoft Fabric, my work spans content and product
          design for CI/CD, CLI, and MCP experiences. I also own the design automation repo our
          30-person design and PM team uses, a system I built from scratch that saw immediate adoption
          and now supports everything from daily prototyping to senior leadership demos.
        </p>
        <p>
          My background is unusual for someone doing this work. I started in journalism and history,
          moved into content and UX writing, and kept pushing further into the technical side until
          I was building agentic workflows, shipping skills to production, and contributing to
          open-source Microsoft tooling. I think that path is a feature: I bridge the human side
          of product problems with the technical side of building systems.
        </p>
        <p>
          On top of that, I've driven org-wide AI initiatives at Microsoft. I initiated a content
          design agent that was adopted and used by 150+ designers, and I was a key contributor to the
          Fabric CLI's AI assets layer, the part the Corporate VP of Product highlighted when
          it shipped GA. I'm also an instructor at the UX Content Collective, where I created
          the Technical Content Designer program.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm part of Content Design Leaders Upstream,
          an invite-only workgroup shaping what UX content becomes in an AI-driven world.
          We compare active fieldwork and build frameworks the broader field can use.
        </p>

        <hr class="divider" />

        <h2>Experience</h2>
        <div class="experience">
          <div class="experience__item">
            <div class="experience__meta">
              <strong>Microsoft</strong>
              <span>February 2022 – present</span>
            </div>
            <p class="experience__role">Senior Content Designer, AI systems and developer experiences</p>
            <p>
              Designing customer-facing content and product experiences for CI/CD, CLI, and MCP tools.
              Building AI-powered workflows and evaluation frameworks for developer and design tools.
              Owner of the team's AI design automation repo and a key contributor to org-wide AI initiatives.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="experience__item">
            <div class="experience__meta">
              <strong>UX Content Collective</strong>
              <span>May 2026 – present</span>
            </div>
            <p class="experience__role">Creator and instructor, Technical Content Designer Program</p>
            <p>Creator and instructor of the Technical Content Designer program, helping content designers build confidence with developer tools and AI systems.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="experience__item">
            <div class="experience__meta">
              <strong>Wix.com</strong>
              <span>2018 – 2022</span>
            </div>
            <p class="experience__role">Senior UX Writer → Accessibility Champion</p>
            <p>
              Lead UX writer and editor for Wix Code. Led content strategy across products,
              coordinated localization for 15+ languages, ran usability testing, and contributed
              to the Words Matter blog. Accessibility champion across the org and hackathon winner.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="experience__item">
            <div class="experience__meta">
              <strong>Natural Intelligence</strong>
              <span>2016 – 2018</span>
            </div>
            <p class="experience__role">Content Manager</p>
            <p>Managed, wrote, and edited content for multiple websites. Used Tableau to run content tests, analyze results, and drive data-informed content decisions.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <hr class="divider" />

        <h2>Education</h2>
        <div class="experience">
          <div class="experience__item">
            <div class="experience__meta">
              <strong>Metropolitan State University of Denver</strong>
              <span>2006 – 2011</span>
            </div>
            <p class="experience__role">BA, History · Minor in Journalism · Helen Verba Award, Society of Professional Journalists</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <hr class="divider" />

        <div class="cta-row">
          <a href="mailto:jeremyd.hoover@gmail.com" class="btn"><Icon name="mail" />Get in touch</a>
        </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .about-page { background: #fff; }
  .about-hero { padding: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.5rem) 0 clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); background: var(--portfolio-blue); color: #fff; }
  .about-id { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.25rem; }
  .about-id img { flex: 0 0 auto; width: 88px; height: 88px; border: 2px solid var(--portfolio-yellow); border-radius: 50%; object-fit: cover; object-position: 50% 30%; box-shadow: var(--elev-2); }
  .about-hero h1 { margin: 0; color: #fff; font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem); line-height: 1.1; }
  .subtitle { margin: 0.35rem 0 0; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.82); font-size: 1rem; max-width: none; }
  .about-content { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem); }
  .about-body p { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); color: var(--portfolio-ink); }
  .experience { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .experience__item { padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--portfolio-radius); background: #fff; box-shadow: var(--elev-1); }
  .experience__meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.25rem 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
  .experience__meta strong { color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-family: var(--f-heading); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .experience__meta span { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.8125rem; }
  .experience__role { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.9375rem; font-weight: 600; max-width: none; }
  .experience__item p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .cta-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-4); }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .about-id img { width: 64px; height: 64px; } }
</style>
